     "texto": [
      "With verbs like **gustar** and **encantar**, the liked thing is the subject and the verb agrees with it:\n\n- Me **gusta** bailar / Me **encanta** cocinar. (activities in infinitive: singular verb)\n- Me **encantan** los libros. (plural noun: plural verb)\n\nTo show who likes something, use indirect object pronouns: **me, te, le, nos, os, les**.\nIf you name the person, precede with **a** and keep the pronoun: **A Pablo le** encanta el fútbol.\n\nTo agree:\n- Positive statement: *Me gusta el cine.* → **A mí también.** (disagree: **A mí no.**)\n- Negative statement: *No me gusta bailar.* → **A mí tampoco.** (disagree: **A mí sí.**)"
